--- !u!114 &1956890467
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1956890466}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d3316448f68d5f05bc3bd94a1e7091a0, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::EinsteinTelescope.Laser.LaserLevel
  title: Long arms
  briefing: 'Long arms: the end test masses now sit in the far towers, almost 16 m from the beam splitter. Walk the beam through Iris A and Iris B, check that it passes Iris X and Iris Y in the middle towers, then align the end mirrors.'
  objectiveText: '1. Steer the beam through Iris A and Iris B with the two steering mirrors.

    2. The beam now runs through the middle towers to the end towers. If it misses Iris X or Iris Y, the input beam is still crooked: go back to step 1.

    3. Align End mirror X and End mirror Y until both beams land in the centre of the output detector.'
  controlsTip: 'The arms are long: use fine mode for the end mirrors. One coarse step moves the spot a long way.'
  physicsText: 'Einstein Telescope will have arms of 10 km. The longer the arm, the further the spot moves for the same tilt of a mirror, so the alignment has to be more precise. That same effect is what makes long arms so sensitive: a tiny change in length becomes measurable.'
  parTimeSeconds: 240
  laser: {fileID: 1859213919}
  mirrors:
  - {fileID: 966596612}
  - {fileID: 1944535833}
  - {fileID: 569298593}
  - {fileID: 46993059}
  checkpoints:
  - {fileID: 1914261313}
  - {fileID: 1312311490}
  - {fileID: 550630893}
  - {fileID: 33434459}
  checkpointLabels:
  - Iris A
  - Iris B
  - Iris X
  - Iris Y
  checkpointHints:
  - 'Beam walking: Steering mirror 1 moves the beam onto Iris A, Steering mirror 2 centres it on Iris B. Repeat until both are centred.'
  - Use Steering mirror 2 to centre the beam on Iris B. If Iris A drifts off, correct it with Steering mirror 1 and come back.
  - Iris X sits in the middle tower of the straight arm. If the beam misses it, straighten the input beam with Steering mirror 1 and 2.
  - Iris Y sits in the middle tower of the reflected arm. If the beam misses it, straighten the input beam with Steering mirror 1 and 2.
  detector: {fileID: 625163222}
